---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { proseClass } from './_seo';
---
<Base pageType="policy" title="Privacy policy | SizeTune" description="What SizeTune does and does not collect: images stay in your browser, there are no accounts, ads or analytics, and the host handles ordinary request data." path="/privacy/">
  <h1 class="mb-3 text-3xl font-bold">Privacy policy</h1>
  <div class={proseClass}>
    <p>Last updated 12 November 2026. [[HUMAN: legal review pending. Have a lawyer review this policy before launch, then replace this marker with the review date or remove it.]]</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      You choose an image, your browser resizes it, and you download the result. SizeTune has no accounts, no ads and no
      analytics scripts at the time of writing. The code of this site does not upload your images.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The site is run by [[HUMAN: owner name or pseudonym that should be shown as the person or business responsible for this site]].
      Questions about privacy can be sent to [[HUMAN: contact email address for privacy questions and requests]]. More about the
      site is on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your images</h2>
    <p>
      When you pick or drop a file, it is read by code running inside your own browser. The resizing, cropping and
      re-encoding happen on your device. SizeTune's code does not send the image, or any part of it, to a server, and we
      keep no copy. When you close the tab, the working data is released by your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some things sit outside the site's control. A browser extension may be able to read pages you open, your device may
      back up files you download, and the file you save goes wherever your browser's download settings put it. Re-saving
      a picture generally drops its camera metadata such as location, but you should check the result if that matters to
      you.
    </p>

    <h2>What the host receives</h2>
    <p>
      The website is delivered by Cloudflare. Like any web host, it receives the ordinary details of each request:
      your IP address, the page address, your browser's user agent, the time and the approximate country. Cloudflare may
      keep such records under its own policies. Our code adds nothing to that, and the requests do not include your
      images.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
    <p>
      The code of this site sets no cookies and does not write to your browser's local storage. Your browser may keep
      ordinary cached copies of the site's files so that pages load faster, which is normal behaviour and not tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics, advertising and search statistics</h2>
    <p>
      SizeTune currently runs no analytics and shows no advertising. The owner uses Google Search Console to see how the
      site appears in Google Search. That service works from Google's own data and does not need any script on these
      pages. If analytics or advertising are ever added, this page will be updated before they go live, with the
      vendors, cookies and your choices described.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Because we hold no images, accounts or profiles, there is very little personal data for us to access, correct or
      delete. If you believe we hold something about you, or you have a concern about this policy, write to the
      contact address above. Where the law gives you rights over your data, you can also contact your local data
      protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We will change this page when the site's behaviour changes and update the date at the top. The terms of use are
      on the <a href="/terms/">terms page</a>, and you can try the tool on the <a href="/">home page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
